# Slice Implementation

When the user asks to implement a slice or you are completing a generated slice:

1. Read **[docs/TEMPLATE.md](../../docs/TEMPLATE.md)** for the full first-slice walkthrough
2. Identify slice type from `packages/slices/src/<SliceName>/slice.json` → `sliceType`
3. Read the plan: `packages/em-slice-generator/<SLICE_TYPE>_POST_GENERATION_PLAN.md`
4. Execute steps in order: decide/evolve, tests, registration in `commands.ts`, `INLINE_PROJECTIONS`, route under `apps/web-app/src/app/api/`, verify

## EM CLI

- `pnpm em:slice:init <Title>`
- `pnpm em:slice:resolve`
- `pnpm em:slice:generate`
- `pnpm em:slice:implement`
- `pnpm em:slice:check-drift --all`

## Plan paths by type

- STATE_CHANGE → `STATE_CHANGE_POST_GENERATION_PLAN.md`
- TRANSLATOR → `TRANSLATOR_POST_GENERATION_PLAN.md`
- AUTOMATION → `AUTOMATION_POST_GENERATION_PLAN.md`
- STATE_VIEW → `STATE_VIEW_POST_GENERATION_PLAN.md`

## Key conventions

- `decide` and `evolve` are pure — no I/O
- Register command handlers in `packages/slices/src/commands.ts`
- Register inline projections in `packages/slices/src/projections-inline.ts`
- Translators use `dispatcher.sendCommand()`, not eventStore directly
- See `docs/SLICE_IMPLEMENTATION_WORKFLOW.md` for full workflow
